==Strategy==
In all of Cat God's appearences, it is necessary to max out the [[Mystery Mask]] treasure ([[Treasure]]s from [[Broton (Cats of the Cosmos)|Broton]], [[N77 Nebula (Cats of the Cosmos)|N77 Nebula]] and [[Black Hole (Cats of the Cosmos)|Black Hole]]) as without these Treasures, he will be buffed to 1,100%, making him impossible to handle reasonably. Since there are also a lot of Starred Aliens, it is recommended to collect all [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]] as well as bringing as many [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|Anti-Alien Cats]] as possible.

==='''Chapter 1'''===
Since The Cat God is a [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy this time, use as many [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|Anti-Floating Cats]] as you can to chip the boss in between his attacks and alien peon waves until he is defeated.

The best strategy is to rush down The Cat God with [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman]], and then lure the enemy peon wave close to your base. Send out your anti-alien crowd controllers and DPS units to quickly kill the peon wave. You want to kill the peons as fast as possible in this stage, so that you don't have to deal with a Spacefish Jones. When you kill a peon wave, don't even bother with meatshielding; just spam Fishman, send out Awakened Bahamut Cat to burst down The Cat God's health in between peon waves. Repeat this, and you should kill The Cat God, and win the stage.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Here [[Cat God]] has 100,000 more HP, and even though he only stands at 300 range now, he has a 1000 range Omni-strike that slows and knockbacks twice, and destroys basically everything with the 3rd hit. There are now also several Kid Tappas and Ribbos which wall your units and warp them respectively. Luckily this stage isn't without its weaknesses. The Ribbos' barrier is their lifeline, so if it gets destroyed they are basically dead. Survive Meatshields work also as the first 2 hits do only 1,998 damage together and all damage is concentrated in the 3rd, allowing them to activate their ability. Additionally the knockbacks can be used to make rebound units hit more times such as A. Bahamut.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
Here [[Final Boss Giga-God]] has only 1 million health, which is less than previous versions, and only 800 range with no Omni-Strike. However he retains the multi hit this time making a level 12 wave that warps everything in the first hit, then nuking everything with his 3rd hit. However, he warps for so long and far that his 3rd hit usually misses. Be careful of the Mesocosmocyclones, as their extreme pushing power can shred your front line. If one has [[Awakened Bahamut Cat]]'s explosion talent, they can chain Final Boss Giga-God's knockbacks (200k damage per knockback, so a level 30+ Bahamut is required if not given support) until another enemy gets in the way.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]] - Very powerful anti-alien attacker that can outrange the majority of the alien peons supporting The Cat God. Just be aware of their cost.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] - Deals heavy damage to The Cat God between peon waves at an affordable price. In chapter 2 & 3 he can still chip him.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] - Very good generalist, especially for this stage due to their high burst damage and Immune to Warp.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - Makes short work of any of the longer ranged threats in this stage if timed correctly between enemy attacks.
*[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] - Has very high freeze uptime and proc chance, paralyzing the peons and allowing your units to take them out without issue. Investing in his freeze up talent will only make the peon waves easier, and allow you much more time to chip down the cat god before the Spacefish Jones arrives.
*[[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Lone Cat and Kitten]] - Can constantly interrupt Cat God's and Final Boss Giga-God's attacks, not letting him attack once as long as you keep the alien peons away.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Twinstars (Uber Rare Cat)|Twinstars]] - Has an only 3900 cost and half the recharge of an average Uber. Can quickly take out the occasional small starred alien waves, and can chip down Project A. and Le' Solar in Ch. 1, and be good support in 2 & 3. Can even take advantage of God 1's lesser damage per hit, God 2's knockback, and God 3's warp to rebound and deal more damage.
*[[Ganglion (Uber Rare Cat)|Ganglion]] - Similar to Twinstars, but instead of a quick recharge & low cost, has EXTREME amounts of damage. His LD can also be used to snipe Le' Solar behind Project A. in Ch. 1, and can quickly take out Ribbo & Kid Tappa in Ch. 2. In Ch. 3, he can nuke and cripple Mesocosmocyclone and the other peons.

